  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed single storey rear extension and first floor rear extension, side roof dormer, together with the proposed enlargement of outbuilding, due to their excessive size and scale, and inappropriate design, would fail to respect the proportions of the host property and would result in bulky and incongruous additions to the site and the wider area, harmful to the overall character and appearance of the site and Heston Village Conservation Area, contrary to the Residential Extensions Guidelines SPD and Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture), CC4 (Heritage), and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed single storey rear extension, due to the excessive size and scale, would harm neighbours' living conditions at 41 Old Cote Drive through an increased sense of enclosure and loss of light and outlook. The proposal therefore fails to comply with adopted Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture), SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations) and the Residential Extension Guidelines as set out within the adopted Character Sustainability and Design Codes SPD."
